    "cost_closing_html":  "Dried chiles and chuck roast make a restaurant dish for grocery money, so the cost tab number stays low. Sale-priced chuck takes it lower still.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eDried chiles are the whole soul of this and they are cheap.\u003c/strong\u003e A bag of guajillo and a bag of ancho cost a few dollars and make several batches. Toast them in a dry pan before you soak them and the flavor jumps.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eChuck roast is the right cut and the budget cut.\u003c/strong\u003e The fat is what makes birria birria, so do not reach for a leaner roast here. Buy it on sale and freeze extra.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSkip the birria paste in a jar.\u003c/strong\u003e Your adobo from whole dried chiles, garlic, and spices costs less and tastes better than the shortcut in the international aisle."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Toast the guajillo and ancho chiles in a dry pan until fragrant, then soak them in hot water until soft and pull the stems and seeds.",
                    "Blend the soaked chiles with the beef broth, garlic, cumin, oregano, and salt into a smooth adobo.",
                    "Brown the chuck, add the diced onion, the bay leaves, and the adobo, cover, and braise until the beef pulls apart with a fork.",
                    "Shred the beef in the pot, fish out the bay leaves, and simmer uncovered a few minutes to thicken the consomme around it.",
                    "Finish the shredded beef with the lime juice and chopped cilantro.",
                    "Lay a warm tortilla, add the portioned beef and a share of the shredded cheese, and roll; crisp it seam down in a dry hot pan for extra credit."
                ],
    "portion_html":  "Set the full pot on your scale and subtract the empty pot weight from Step 1. That is your total shredded-beef weight. Divide it by 14, spoon that amount onto each warm tortilla, add an even share of the cheese, and roll. Every burrito lands at about \u003cstrong\u003e395 calories and 32 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e.",
